---
// The small icon, an arrow leaving a box, that tells a sighted reader a link
// opens in a new window. It is the sight half of the warning (WCAG 3.2.5): the
// words, in the link's name, are the other, so the icon is hidden from the
// accessibility tree and a screen reader hears them once. It is drawn inline in
// currentColor, so it takes the colour of whatever it sits in, including where
// colours are forced, and its few lines are this site's own. Keeping it with
// the word before it is the link's to do (see OutsideLink.astro). Without it a
// link that leaves the site would look like one that does not, and each place
// that has one would draw its own.
---

<svg
  class="new-window-icon"
  viewBox="0 0 16 16"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.75"
  stroke-linecap="square"
  stroke-linejoin="miter"
  focusable="false"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <path d="M7 2.5H2.5v11h11V9" />
  <path d="M9.5 2.5h4v4" />
  <path d="M13.5 2.5 7 9" />
</svg>
